## Why This Is Asked
Tests knowledge of low-level synchronization, memory ordering, and backoff strategies under contention. Also checks ability to translate theory into working code and simple performance measurement.

## Key Concepts
- C11 atomics and memory_order_acquire/release
- atomic_flag spinlocks and their correctness
- exponential backoff to prevent livelock
- basic contention metrics (wall time, backoffs)

## Code Example
```javascript
#include <stdatomic.h>
#include <emmintrin.h>

static atomic_uint counter = 0;
static atomic_flag lock = ATOMIC_FLAG_INIT;

void lock_spin() {
  unsigned int backoff = 1;
  while (atomic_flag_test_and_set_explicit(&lock, memory_order_acquire)) {
    _mm_pause();
    if (backoff < 1024) backoff <<= 1;
    for (volatile unsigned int i = 0; i < backoff; ++i) _mm_pause();
  }
}

void unlock_spin() {
  atomic_flag_clear_explicit(&lock, memory_order_release);
}
```

